    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d811">

                <pb facs="1276" n="1262" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1262"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/11–744: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé to the Czechoslovak Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-07T19:00:00+01:00">November 7, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Zecho 22. In note of November 6 Czechoslovak Foreign Office states German radio
                    reports recent capture in Slovakia of Czech General Viest and Brigadier General
                    Golian together with other officers, and soldiers. Czech Government appeals to
                    United States Government again to issue in any suitable form a warning to German
                    military and other authorities against mistreatment of war prisoners in line
                    with its declaration of September 7.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d811-f1"/> Similar
                    appeal is being addressed to British and Soviet Governments.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Schoenfeld</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d811-f1" n="55" xml:id="d811-f1-content">
                <p>Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, September 10, 1944, p.
